From f13c96b8f58dc21f4e608043539aa8e2ffbaf8fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:39:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: skip dead object entries in the Lunal mode take routine

The Lunal mode take routine tried to skip dead entries of the object
list with a test on the address of the kind record, which is never
NULL, so entries that had been forgotten (zeroed, kind 0) were treated
like live ones. Their location is (0,0), the corner of the level, and
when that grid was in view it became a flow target alongside the real
items, so the Borg could step towards the corner instead of the item.
Test the kind index, as the other take routines do.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#72.

(cherry picked from commit 9492d74ce57ae63fca41866113bc7f35463c5704)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-take.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
index c5243ddd6..9c2baf06a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
@@ -739,7 +739,7 @@ bool borg_flow_take_lunal(bool viewable, int nearness)
         bool item_bad;
 
         /* Skip dead objects */
-        if (!k_ptr)
+        if (!take->kidx)
             continue;
 
         /* Access the location */
-- 
